"# Late night return to the book thing\nBecause I was turning the async stuff around in my mind, right?\nLooking for other ways to speed it up\nPondering one thing that I probably had done right but possibly hadn’t\n\nAnd then it hit me\n*I donked it up*\n\n![](dayone-moment:\/\/2E8104417AD24BF0AF85DC504F3B041A)\n\nSee, I thought I’d been clever\nThis one centerpiece, the template renderer, at the center of everything\nReading in the template files and processing with them\nAnd I’d set it up to cache the template files it read\nSo that it only read the template files once\n\nAnd I thought, wow, gee whiz, now it won’t keep reading the same damn files over and over again, the same tag files for every damn entry, the same entry files for every damn entry, over and over again\n\nExcept\nExcept except except\n\n        ```\nconst absolutePath = path\\.resolve\\(templatePath\\);\n```\n\n        ```\nconst source = await fs\\.promises\\.readFile\\(absolutePath, \"utf8\"\\);\n```\n\n        ```\ntemplate = Handlebars\\.compile\\(source, \\{\n```\n\n            ```\nnoEscape: true, \/\/ important for CSS \/ raw text\n```\n\n            ```\nstrict: true,\n```\n\n        ```\n\\}\\);\n```\n\n        ```\ncache\\[absolutePath\\] = template;\n```\n\n\n\\.\\.\\.There’s an “await” before the cache happens\nWhich means they don’t get cached immediately, the caching is deferred as the cue fills *right up*\nWhich means\nIf we add a friendly little `console\\.log\\( Reading '$\\{templatePath\\}'\\.\\.\\. \\);` in there\\.\\.\\.\\.\n\n![](dayone-moment:\/\/E9866CD50AD048E4944DCDF9CAC30710)\n\n![](dayone-moment:\/\/2FA3C2E8D38442E9AF8EC54D1BF4EB5A)\n\n![](dayone-moment:\/\/79548AE08F204142A7F84DF9DB1DD56C)\n\nA million billion file reads\nA million billion accesses of the file system\nTo read the same SEVEN FILES\nOver and over again\\.\n\nSo uh\nLet’s fix that\\.\n\n\\(Incidentally, for comparison, I measure the current execution time to be something like 5\\.3, 5\\.4 seconds\\. And there’s a noticeable delay before it actually starts burning through entries\\.\\)\n\nOh, I even fucked up the saving of the file \\- I check the cache for `templatePath` , but save to it under `absolutePath` \\.\n\nSo okay\nA little revision later\\.\\.\\.\n\n![](dayone-moment:\/\/5B9C94671FF74750B095B5A4E52B5955)\n\nAnd *voila\\!*\n\n![](dayone-moment:\/\/329723BFC2534CBC9F6A5EE0081FB6B9)\n\nOne file read per file\\.\n\nAnd an average time of abooooouuuuuut\\.\\.\\.\\. 3\\.7 seconds\\.\nWe’ve gone down from 5\\.3 to 3\\.7\nAnd actually, I ought to check the original times before I did any async at all\\.\\.\\.\nLooks like 6\\.2 seconds?\nI’ve basically cut execution time in half\n\nAnd given my percentages list basically all shows up at once, I really don’t need it anymore\\.\n\nIt’s also used in the test thing that turns the journal into entries, and at least you can see them coming through one at a time there, but even that is super fast\\.\nSo\nLet’s clean house\\.\n\n---\n\nOh right\nRegex\nI’m instantiating the same regex literals over and over again every time my “process” rules run I wonder if it would make a difference to store those too\\.\n\nIt probably won’t, but it’s probably good to do anyway\\.\n\n\\.\\.\\.yeah, still ~3\\.6s\nOh well\nGood to have done\\.\nProbably?\n\n---\n\nNow it’s 11:00 and I’m just rewriting test stuff as asynchronous for the fun of it\\.\n\n---\n\nOkay it’s 11:10 and i need to go to bed\\."
